Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.1
Published by Google Cloud, in GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog
    https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/blob/main/okf/SPEC.md
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The knowledge-vault subsystem produces bundles in the Open Knowledge Format, an
open specification published by Google Cloud. OKF defines the portable format:
a directory of Markdown files with YAML frontmatter, `type` as the only required
field, the reserved filenames `index.md` and `log.md`, and cross-links that form
a graph.

OKF does NOT define, and is not the source of, the verification layer this
harness adds on top of it: the `verified_against` commit stamp, the manifest
used as an ID registry and reverse index, the link allowlist, the concept size
budget, or a validator that rejects. Those are this project's work,
MIT-licensed, and must not be attributed to Google or to the OKF specification.

Body sections are a shared case rather than a clean split. OKF §4.2 defines
`Schema`, `Examples` and `Citations` as conventional headings that SHOULD be
used when applicable, and states there are no required body sections. Turning
those into a fixed, ordered, per-type sequence that a validator enforces is this
project's addition; the vocabulary itself is OKF's.

On conformance: OKF §9 makes conformance a property of a bundle, with three
producer-side conditions (parseable frontmatter on every non-reserved file, a
non-empty `type` in each, and reserved filenames following §6 and §7). Separately
it directs consumers not to reject a bundle over missing optional fields, unknown
types or keys, broken links, or absent index files. This project's extra rules
bind producers and sit above the §9 floor, so they add strictness without
breaching it: a bundle produced under them still satisfies all three conditions
and remains conformant. Note that the bundle-root `index.md` carries frontmatter
in order to declare `okf_version`, which §11 permits as the sole exception to
index files having none.

